  "findings": {
    "publicParse": "Ratio-of-medians -7.70%, paired median -7.78%, 11/15 faster. Direction agrees with count1 (-8.19% ratio; 13/15 faster), but count16 paired descriptive95 interval [-11.69%,+1.95%] crosses zero. Evidence supports a directional improvement, not a statistically settled exact speedup.",
    "negativeControls": "Unchanged typed parse shifts -1.11% ratio, -1.63% paired, 11/15 faster; descriptive interval [-5.90%,-0.18%]. This is much smaller than its count1 -8.56% ratio, but not exactly zero. Source shifts -2.21% ratio while paired median is +0.11%, interval [-3.26%,+1.86%]; ratio alone misstates paired consistency.",
    "attribution": "Deterministic allocation reductions remain the direct mechanism proof. This follow-up strengthens the directional latency observation relative to count1 confounding, but cannot assign all measured public-parse change to removed allocations. Do not subtract typed or source shifts from public parse.",
    "host": "Same Apple M1 Pro/darwin/arm64; different time and host process/load state. Recorded interactive/background services remain active. No claim of an otherwise idle machine.",
    "limitations": "One medium Gantt workload; no count16 retained/mutable rows and no new browser/Swift evidence. Batching does not establish cold single-operation latency. Preserve count1 raw report and caveats."
